---
import Section from '../Section.astro';
import Container from '../Container.astro';
import SectionHeader from '../SectionHeader.astro';

/*
  Pitch page section 5 — the model (docs/pitch-demo-sitemap.md §4.5, owner-required).

  NO NUMBERS, NO CHARTS, NO UNIT ECONOMICS — the sitemap's integrity flag for
  this section and `creative-director`'s review both land in the same place: a
  revenue projection, a cohort curve or a unit-economics table rendered on a page
  reads as reported results. This section carries the mechanic only.

  DATA GAP (owner): the membership price, and whether the gathering layer is
  included, ticketed, or both. The mechanic can be shown without it; the section
  cannot be called finished until it is answered.

  REMOVED (2026-09-10, site owner): the four-node loop diagram (content → room →
  relationship → retention) and its lorem ipsum caption. The section now runs
  straight from the two prose paragraphs into The Vibe, with nothing placeholder
  in between.

  COPY STATUS: the two prose paragraphs are real, owner-supplied copy (2026-09-09) —
  the Gaia-demand argument and the "reserved vs. bold" positioning.

  STRUCTURE NOTE: the header sits outside `.prose` deliberately, matching every
  other pitch section (Problem, Vibe, Plan, Who). This section originally nested
  SectionHeader inside `.prose`'s own flex column, so SectionHeader's own 64px
  margin-bottom stacked with `.prose`'s 24px gap into an 88px gap under the
  heading — visibly too much space, reported and fixed 2026-09-10. Every other
  section keeps the header out of any gapped flex/grid container for exactly
  this reason; keep it that way here too, or the double-count comes back.
*/
---

<Section tone="deep" id="model">
  <Container>
    <SectionHeader kicker="The model" heading="Every dimension, one membership." />

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        <a class="gaia-link" href="https://www.gaia.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Gaia</a> has already proven that there is enough demand for conscious media within
        the spiritually awakened community to build a global company. And while it
        may seem that Gaia has a stronghold on the conscious media production and
        distribution space, there is an entire demographic that Gaia is missing, perhaps
        intentionally.
      </p>
      <p>
        Gaia’s communications and programming have traditionally been reserved,
        restrained, and passive. This leaves room for another platform built on a similar
        model, but with a voice and identity that are more fun, creative, bold, and daring.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Container>
</Section>

<style>
  .prose {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-6);
    color: var(--color-text-body);
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  /* Inline links inherit color and lose their underline globally (global.css) —
     fine for nav/button links that are already visually distinct chrome, not
     for a link sitting inside a paragraph of body text, where color alone
     would be the only signal. Underlined + the site's one accent color, so it
     reads as a link without spending a second visual language on it. */
  .gaia-link {
    color: var(--color-electric-cyan);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: currentColor;
  }
</style>
